<?xml version="1.0"?>
<document>
  <properties>
    <title>Flattening a relative-path parent chain</title>
  </properties>

  <body>
    <section name="Flattening a relative-path parent chain">
      <p>
        A project can inherit shared build configuration through one or more parents that exist only in the source
        repository. Set <code>flattenRelativePathParent</code> to merge that complete local parent chain into the
        flattened POM instead of publishing references to build-only POMs. The first parent that is not resolved from
        the filesystem is retained as the published parent.
      </p>

      <subsection name="Repository-wide parent">
        <p>
          The repository-wide parent has fixed coordinates and inherits from a stable published parent. Its empty
          <code>relativePath</code> marks the end of the local chain. It also configures the flatten plugin once for
          every project using this layout.
        </p>
        <source><![CDATA[
<project>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <parent>
    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>published-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2.0.0</version>
    <relativePath/>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>repository-common-parent</artifactId>
  <version>LOCAL</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>

  <properties>
    <repository.property>repository-value</repository.property>
  </properties>

  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.codehaus.mojo</groupId>
        <artifactId>flatten-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <flattenMode>resolveCiFriendliesOnly</flattenMode>
          <flattenRelativePathParent>true</flattenRelativePathParent>
        </configuration>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <id>flatten</id>
            <phase>process-resources</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>flatten</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
          <execution>
            <id>flatten.clean</id>
            <goals>
              <goal>clean</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
        ]]></source>
      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Module-specific parent">
        <p>
          A second repository-only parent can add configuration for one module or a group of modules. Its parent is
          resolved from another source-tree POM, so both local layers will be collapsed.
        </p>
        <source><![CDATA[
<project>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <parent>
    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>repository-common-parent</artifactId>
    <version>LOCAL</version>
    <relativePath>../common-pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>library-common-parent</artifactId>
  <version>LOCAL</version>
  <packaging>pom</packaging>

  <properties>
    <module.property>module-value</module.property>
  </properties>
</project>
        ]]></source>
      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Published child">
        <p>
          The child points to its nearest repository-only parent explicitly. The coordinates in every local parent
          reference must match the POM found at its <code>relativePath</code>.
        </p>
        <source><![CDATA[
<project>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <parent>
    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>library-common-parent</artifactId>
    <version>LOCAL</version>
    <relativePath>common-pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>example-library</artifactId>
  <version>${revision}</version>
</project>
        ]]></source>

        <p>The installed or deployed POM contains both inherited property sets and the published parent:</p>
        <source><![CDATA[
<project>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <parent>
    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>published-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2.0.0</version>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>example-library</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.0</version>
  <properties>
    <repository.property>repository-value</repository.property>
    <module.property>module-value</module.property>
  </properties>
</project>
        ]]></source>
        <p>
          Neither repository-only parent nor the <code>flattenRelativePathParent</code> control flag is published. An
          empty <code>relativePath</code> on the child's immediate parent is rejected because there is no local parent
          to collapse. On a higher parent it ends the local chain and leaves that parent for repository resolution.
        </p>
      </subsection>
    </section>
  </body>
</document>
